codec4AI packages video-loader 0.3.0.
Original package author: Turing VLA.
The project source and FFmpeg reference-graph modifications are distributed
under GPL-3.0-or-later. See LICENSE.

Bundled binary wheels include modified FFmpeg, x264, x265 and libaom.
Their original notices and terms are retained in licenses/ and in the
corresponding upstream source archives shipped alongside each release.
pybind11 headers are used to compile the Python extension (BSD-3-Clause).
NumPy is a separately installed runtime dependency; it is not vendored.

FFmpeg modifications: tools/patches/ffmpeg-8.1.2-reference-graph.patch adds
private H.264/HEVC reference-graph callbacks and state-only decoding.
The release build adds change notices to the modified files (2026-09-29).
Upstream encoder sources are used without the private b31 modifications.

This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group
(FFmpeg's upstream attribution; see FFmpeg LICENSE.md in the source archive).

The exact source inputs, hashes and reconstruction instructions are in
tools/sources.json, tools/build_native_deps.py and docs/BUILDING.md.
Distribute the corresponding-sources archive and source distribution with
the wheel. See docs/RELEASING.md for release contents.
